  "plain": "In the 1950s and 60s the United States had a plan called Project Orion to push a spacecraft with nuclear explosions, and Michels says the Air Force general Curtis LeMay wanted it and the physicist Freeman Dyson worked on it. He says John F. Kennedy was strongly against it, so it was killed. Michels tells this himself, without naming a source, in a conversation with a former Secretary of Energy, as an example of bold propulsion ideas that were shelved."
